# Git Workflow

- **Branch naming**: `feature/<card>-<short-desc>` (e.g.
  `feature/channel-ch1-sine-test`), `fix/<short-desc>` for bug fixes.
- **Commit messages**: imperative subject line + a short rationale paragraph,
  matching the descriptive style already used in this repo (e.g.
  `Initial commit: known-good Channel and Effect card firmware baseline.`).
  Explain *why*, especially for hardware workarounds — future readers (and
  future agents) can't see the oscilloscope trace that justified a change.
- **Never commit `build/` output.** Already covered by the per-project
  `apps/channel_card/.gitignore` / `apps/effect_card/.gitignore` (`build`,
  `mx.scratch`) — don't `git add -f` around it.
- **`.ioc`-derived regenerated files** (`cmake/stm32cubemx/**`) should only be
  committed alongside a note in the commit body confirming the post-regen
  checklist (`stm32-cubemx-workflow.mdc`) was run.
- **Small, reviewable commits/PRs per feature** — don't mix rule/doc changes
  with firmware behavior changes in the same commit.
- Run a `git diff` before committing generated-adjacent files; a regeneration
  silently deleting hand-written code is a real, previously-hit failure mode
  on this project.
